# Python virtual environments
.venv/
**/.venv/

# Generated reference vectors for the C++ planner port (docs/port_workflow.md).
# The GENERATORS are tracked — web/test/port/cppRef*.test.ts — and are the only
# definition of these files. The outputs are large (discretize_ref.txt alone is
# 10 MB), fully reproducible, and would otherwise be re-committed on every
# fixture change, so they are built on demand instead:
#
#     cd web && GEN_CPP_REF=1 npx vitest run test/port
#
# Every test that reads one fails with that command in its message if it is
# missing, so an ungenerated checkout says so rather than passing over no data.
#
# test/data/svg_fixtures.txt is deliberately NOT ignored. It is 496 bytes of
# INPUT geometry, not answers, and it is the one generated file the CONTRACT
# suite reads — so tracking it keeps that suite runnable on a fresh clone with
# no generator run, which is the state the port lands in once bit-parity
# retires.
test/data/*_ref.txt
